.TH COMPRESS-JXL 1 "2026-11-08" "2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
compress-jxl \- batch compress images to JPEG XL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B compress-jxl.sh
[\fB\-q\fR \fIquality\fP]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIeffort\fP]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIWxH\fP|\fBnone\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIthreads\fP]
[\fB\-c\fP]
[\fB\-l\fP]
[\fIdirectory\fP | \fIquality\fP [\fIeffort\fP]]
.br
.B compress-jxl.sh
[\fB\-h\fP | \fB\-\-help\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively finds all \fB.jpg\fP, \fB.jpeg\fP, and \fB.png\fP files under
the target directory and converts them to JPEG XL (\fB.jxl\fP) using
.BR cjxl (1).
Images are left at their original resolution by default.
If a target box is supplied with \fB\-s\fP, images whose width or height
exceeds it are downscaled to fit inside it with the aspect ratio unchanged.
The original file is replaced only if the compressed output is smaller.
Directories named
.B Cooking
under the target are skipped.
.P
Metadata is preserved without relying on external tag copies.
Native EXIF, XMP, ICC profiles, and alpha channels are carried into the
JXL container by \fBcjxl\fP itself.
PNG text chunks used by AI generators (for example
.BR Parameters ,
.BR Prompt ,
.B Workflow ,
.BR Comment ,
and
.BR Description )
are read directly from the PNG and re-embedded as properties in a private
XMP namespace, so tag names and values survive byte-for-byte, including
multi-hundred-kilobyte ComfyUI workflow JSON.
Because a downscale is performed on a temporary file, the scanner also
extracts the original EXIF and XMP blocks and passes them back to
\fBcjxl\fP, so resized outputs keep their metadata too.
.P
Requirements: \fBcjxl\fP and \fBpython3\fP.
Downscaling uses \fBvipsthumbnail\fP (libvips) when available and falls
back to ImageMagick's \fBconvert\fP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " \fIquality\fP"
Quality target (0\(en100, default: 85).
Higher = larger file, better fidelity.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-effort " \fIeffort\fP"
Encoder effort (1\(en10, default: 3).
Higher = slower encode, generally more accurate quality at the same
nominal setting.
.RS
.PD 0
.TP
1\(en2  lightning, decent compression
.TP
3\(en4  fast, best size/time knee for batch runs
.TP
5\(en6  balanced, about 4\(mu6\(mu slower
.TP
7     default cjxl speed, very good compression
.TP
8\(en10  exhaustive, noticeably slower
.PD
.RE
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " \fIWxH\fP|\fBnone\fR"
Maximum output dimensions (default: \fBnone\fP, no downscaling).
When \fIWxH\fP is given, larger images are scaled to fit within the box
while keeping their aspect ratio; the image is never enlarged.
Use \fBnone\fP (or \fB0\fP) to make this explicit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threads " \fIthreads\fP"
Parallel encode jobs (default: one per CPU core).
When four or more jobs run, each \fBcjxl\fP process is limited to one
thread to avoid oversubscription; with fewer jobs each process uses all
cores.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compare
Save a lossless PNG copy of each pre-encode source to
\fB/tmp/jxl_compare_src/\fP for later quality comparison
with tools like
.BR ssimulacra2 (1)
or
.BR butteraugli (1).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log
Append a per-run summary line to \fB.compress-jxl.log\fP in the target
directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.PD 0
.TP
.I directory
Target directory (default: \fB~/Pictures/img/Downloads\fP).
If relative, resolved under the default root.
.TP
.I quality
Numeric quality (0\(en100). If the first positional argument is a
number, it is treated as quality, not a directory.
.TP
.I effort
Numeric effort (1\(en10). Must follow a numeric quality.
.PD
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
compress-jxl.sh
Run with defaults: quality 85, effort 3, no downscaling,
\fB~/Pictures/img/Downloads\fP.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh 80
Quality 80, effort 3, default directory.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh 90 5
Quality 90, effort 5, default directory.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh ~/Pictures/wallpapers 80 5
Custom directory, quality 80, effort 5.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh -q 75 -e 3 -t 6 -c ~/ai_art
Quality 75, effort 3, 6 parallel jobs, save comparison sources.
.TP
compress-jxl.sh -s 1920x1080 ~/Pictures/wallpapers
Downscale to fit 1080p instead of the default (no downscaling).
.TP
compress-jxl.sh -s 2560x2560 ~/Pictures/archive
Cap the long edge at 2560 px for every orientation.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
Each file is encoded to a temporary name and moved into place only after
a successful encode, so an interrupted run never leaves a partial
\fB.jxl\fP.
The output inherits the source file's modification time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/img/Downloads/.compress-jxl.log
Per-run summary appended after each batch when \fB\-l\fP is used.
.TP
.I /tmp/jxl_compare_src/
Directory holding pre-encode PNGs when \fB\-c\fP is used.
.TP
.I /tmp/jxl_meta_\fIpid\fP/
Temporary EXIF/XMP sidecars used during a run; removed on exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cjxl (1),
.BR djxl (1),
.BR jxlinfo (1),
.BR ssimulacra2 (1)
